      en: "The Citadel of Tabriz (Arg-e Alishah) is a historical fortress ruin in central Tabriz, Iran. Originally built in the 14th century as a mosque under the Ilkhanid ruler Alishah, it was later converted into a citadel. The massive structure is made of brick and mortar, with an impressive wall up to 28 meters high. It served as a military base during the Safavid and Qajar periods. In the 19th century, it was occupied by Russian troops. Today it is a symbol of the city and a national heritage site. The citadel is part of the historic bazaar complex, a UNESCO World Heritage site.",
