      en: "The Tomb of Esther and Mordechai in Hamadan is one of the most sacred Jewish sites in Iran. According to tradition, it houses the remains of Queen Esther and her cousin Mordechai, key figures in the biblical Book of Esther. The current structure dates back to the 13th century, with a domed chamber adorned with Hebrew inscriptions. The site has undergone several renovations, including a major restoration in the 1970s. It serves as a pilgrimage destination for Iranian Jews and attracts tourists interested in Persian-Jewish history. The tomb stands as a testament to the long-standing Jewish presence in Iran.",
