      en: "The Haruniyyeh Dome (Gonbad-e Haruniyyeh) is a historical structure in Tus, Razavi Khorasan Province, dating to the 13th century, part of a larger archaeological complex. Its exact function is debated; may have been a mausoleum or mosque. The octagonal brick building features a tall dome reminiscent of Central Asian architecture. It is associated with the poet Ferdowsi, who is buried in Tus. The dome is a significant example of Islamic architecture during the Ilkhanid period.",
