      en: "Babak Castle (Qal'eh-e Babak) is located in the forested mountains of Arasbaran in northwestern Iran. The fortress dates back to the 9th century and was the last stronghold of the Khurramite leader Babak Khorramdin, who fought against the Abbasid Caliphate until his capture in 837 CE. The castle sits atop a 2,700-meter peak, offering spectacular views. Ruins include walls, towers, and cisterns. The hike to the castle is a popular trekking route. The site symbolizes resistance and is a national heritage landmark.",
